er-window-management/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47388137","date_published":"2026-03-15T15:09:24Z","author":{"name":"dpassens","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=dpassens"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47387047","title":"Glassworm Is Back: A New Wave of Invisible Unicode Attacks Hits Repositories","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.aikido.dev/blog/glassworm-returns-unicode-attack-github-npm-vscode\"\u003ehttps://www.aikido.dev/blog/glassworm-returns-unicode-attack-github-npm-vscode\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47387047\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47387047\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 202\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 118\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.aikido.dev/blog/glassworm-returns-unicode-attack-github-npm-vscode","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47387047","date_published":"2026-03-15T13:08:02Z","author":{"name":"robinhouston","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=robinhouston"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386908","title":"Harold and George Destroy the World","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://tomclancy.info/harold-and-george.html\"\u003ehttps://tomclancy.info/harold-and-george.html\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386908\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386908\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 222\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 274\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://tomclancy.info/harold-and-george.html","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386908","date_published":"2026-03-15T12:48:17Z","author":{"name":"tclancy","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=tclancy"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386856","title":"Hollywood Enters Oscars Weekend in Existential Crisis","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.theculturenewspaper.com/hollywood-enters-oscars-weekend-in-existential-crisis/\"\u003ehttps://www.theculturenewspaper.com/hollywood-enters-oscars-weekend-in-existential-crisis/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386856\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386856\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 115\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 369\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.theculturenewspaper.com/hollywood-enters-oscars-weekend-in-existential-crisis/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386856","date_published":"2026-03-15T12:41:56Z","author":{"name":"RickJWagner","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=RickJWagner"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386813","title":"I'm 60 years old. Claude Code killed a passion","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eI stumble upon a post from shannoncc called \"I'm 60 years old. Claude Code has re-ignited a passion\", and it made me think. I am also (almost) 60, but AI just killed the passion. I remember all the pre-AI days, where I was enjoying coding during the day, the evening, the weekends and the vacations. This is no more, while others have their \"passion re-ignited\".\u003cp\u003eI would argue it depends on what you enjoy: the journey or the destination. I have always enjoyed the journey, I think people having a blast nowadays are enjoying the destination. AI gave us more destinations, but less journey. It is not worse or better, just different.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386813\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386813\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 185\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 152\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386813","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386813","date_published":"2026-03-15T12:35:22Z","author":{"name":"fred1268","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=fred1268"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386651","title":"Pentagon expands oversight of Stars and Stripes, limits content","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.stripes.com/theaters/us/2026-03-13/pentagon-modernization-plan-stars-and-stripes-21051529.html\"\u003ehttps://www.stripes.com/theaters/us/2026-03-13/pentagon-modernization-plan-stars-and-stripes-21051529.html\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386651\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386651\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 164\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 80\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.stripes.com/theaters/us/2026-03-13/pentagon-modernization-plan-stars-and-stripes-21051529.html","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386651","date_published":"2026-03-15T12:11:32Z","author":{"name":"geox","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=geox"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386636","title":"The 100 hour gap between a vibecoded prototype and a working product","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://kanfa.macbudkowski.com/vibecoding-cryptosaurus\"\u003ehttps://kanfa.macbudkowski.com/vibecoding-cryptosaurus\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386636\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386636\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 224\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 301\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://kanfa.macbudkowski.com/vibecoding-cryptosaurus","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386636","date_published":"2026-03-15T12:09:30Z","author":{"name":"kiwieater","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=kiwieater"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386581","title":"Show HN: Signet – Autonomous wildfire tracking from satellite and weather data","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eI built Signet in Go to see if an autonomous system could handle the wildfire monitoring loop that people currently run by hand - checking satellite feeds, pulling up weather, looking at terrain and fuels, deciding whether a detection is actually a fire worth tracking.\u003cp\u003eAll the data already exists: NASA FIRMS thermal detections, GOES-19 imagery, NWS forecasts, LANDFIRE fuel models, USGS elevation, Census population data, OpenStreetMap. The problem is it arrives from different sources on different cadences in different formats.\u003cp\u003eMost of the system is deterministic plumbing - ingestion, spatial indexing, deduplication. I use Gemini to orchestrate 23 tools across weather, terrain, imagery, and incident tracking for the part where clean rules break down: deciding which weak detections are worth investigating, what context to pull next, and how to synthesize noisy evidence into a structured assessment.\u003cp\u003eIt also records time-bounded predictions and scores them against later data, so the system is making falsifiable claims instead of narrating after the fact. The current prediction metrics are visible on the site even though the sample is still small.\u003cp\u003eIt's already opening incidents from raw satellite detections and matching some to official NIFC reporting. But false positives, detection latency, and incident matching can still be rough.\u003cp\u003eI'd especially welcome criticism on: where should this be more deterministic instead of LLM-driven? And is this kind of autonomous monitoring actually useful, or just noisier than doing it by hand?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386581\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386581\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 103\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 29\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://signet.watch","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386581","date_published":"2026-03-15T12:01:00Z","author":{"name":"mapldx","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=mapldx"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386116","title":"A Visual Introduction to Machine Learning (2015)","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://r2d3.us/visual-intro-to-machine-learning-part-1/\"\u003ehttps://r2d3.us/visual-intro-to-machine-learning-part-1/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386116\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386116\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 305\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 29\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://r2d3.us/visual-intro-to-machine-learning-part-1/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47386116","date_published":"2026-03-15T10:47:35Z","author":{"name":"vismit2000","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=vismit2000"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47385935","title":"$96 3D-printed rocket that recalculates its mid-air trajectory using a $5 sensor","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/novatic14/MANPADS-System-Launcher-and-Rocket\"\u003ehttps://github.com/novatic14/MANPADS-System-Launcher-and-Rocket\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47385935\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47385935\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 374\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 336\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://github.com/novatic14/MANPADS-System-Launcher-and-Rocket","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47385935","date_published":"2026-03-15T10:15:47Z","author":{"name":"ZacnyLos","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=ZacnyLos"}}]}